From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Henrik Klee <henrik@goat-code.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:58:38 +0800
Subject: [PATCH] usb: dwc2: params: Use 16-word DMA bursts on Apple SoCs

The default leaves the DMA burst length at INCR, which holds bulk OUT to about
20 MiB/s through the small receive FIFO on the A10. m1n1 on the same controller
uses INCR16 and reaches over 35 MiB/s.

Assisted-by: LLM
---
 drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
index c6be27724cfe..de10ca04c433 100644
--- a/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
+++ b/drivers/usb/dwc2/params.c
@@ -314,7 +314,8 @@ static void dwc2_set_apple_silicon_params(struct dwc2_hsotg *hsotg)
 	p->host_nperio_tx_fifo_size = 16;
 	p->g_np_tx_fifo_size = 16;
 	p->lpm = false;
-
+	/* As m1n1 runs it on the same controller; shorter bursts hold bulk OUT to about 20 MiB/s. */
+	p->ahbcfg = GAHBCFG_HBSTLEN_INCR16 << GAHBCFG_HBSTLEN_SHIFT;
 
 	fifo_count = dwc2_hsotg_tx_fifo_count(hsotg);
 	p->g_tx_fifo_size[0] = 64;
